    question_en: "A regional airline operates an online flight booking and check-in platform. During the online check-in process, passengers upload travel identity documents (such as passports and entry visas) to an Amazon S3 bucket. The airline requires an automated solution to validate the uploaded documents against passenger booking records, extract metadata, and update an Amazon DynamoDB table. Any verification failures must be routed to an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) dead-letter queue (DLQ) for manual review by customer support agents. Processing each document takes approximately 3 to 5 seconds. The submission volume fluctuates drastically, experiencing heavy surges during holiday promotional fare sales and near-zero activity during off-peak overnight hours. A solutions architect must design an architecture that scales automatically to handle traffic spikes, incurs no compute costs during idle periods, and requires the LEAST operational overhead.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements?",
