    question_en: "A mobile game studio is preparing to release a new competitive turn-based mobile game. At the end of every match, the game client uploads a compressed match telemetry and replay file (averaging 2 MB) directly to an Amazon S3 bucket. The studio requires an automated solution to extract player statistics from each file, perform basic anti-cheat verification, and record the finalized match results into an Amazon DynamoDB table. Each file takes approximately 10 to 20 seconds to process.\n\nTraffic follows unpredictable patterns, spiking dramatically during in-game weekend tournaments and dropping to nearly zero during weekday maintenance periods. The studio has a small engineering team and wants a solution that processes uploads immediately, incurs no infrastructure costs during periods of inactivity, and requires the LEAST operational overhead.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements?",
