    question_en: "A mobile game studio recently released a global multiplayer action game. The game client downloads dynamic patches, high-resolution texture packs, and audio assets totaling over 15 TB from a single Amazon S3 bucket located in the us-east-1 Region. Players in the Asia-Pacific and European regions report slow download speeds and frequent connection timeouts during game launches and seasonal updates. Additionally, the studio's security policy mandates that the S3 bucket remain private and inaccessible directly from the public internet to prevent unauthorized asset scraping.\n\nWhich combination of actions should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements with the LOWEST latency and MINIMAL operational overhead?",
