    question_en: "A mobile game studio is launching a new multiplayer game. The backend includes an ingestion service that handles player score submissions and reward redemption events. When popular gaming influencers host live stream events, the service experiences sudden, unpredictable traffic surges of millions of requests within seconds, followed by long periods of low activity. During previous playtests, these sudden spikes overwhelmed the backend servers, leading to dropped requests and database write timeouts. \n\nA solutions architect must redesign the architecture to reliably absorb unpredictable traffic spikes without losing requests, scale compute and database resources automatically, and minimize operational overhead.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements?",
