    question_en: "A healthcare startup, Nexura Health, operates a multi-tenant platform that allows partner clinics and medical laboratories to query electronic health records (EHR) via an Amazon API Gateway REST API backed by AWS Lambda functions. During peak operating hours, one large hospital network sent an overwhelming volume of automated requests, causing the API Gateway regional account-level throttle limits to be reached and degrading service availability for other partner clinics.\n\nTo resolve this issue, the startup wants to introduce three distinct partner tiers (Standard, Professional, and Enterprise). Each tier must have a specific allowed request rate (requests per second) and an overall monthly request quota. The solution must identify each partner individually, enforce the tier limits to prevent any single client from exhausting backend capacity, and require the LEAST operational overhead.\n\nWhich solution should a solutions architect recommend?",
