    question_en: "A regional airline operates an online flight reservation platform with a relational database running on an Amazon EC2 instance backed by an Amazon EBS gp3 volume in a single Availability Zone. As part of its business continuity strategy and load-testing procedures, the airline regularly takes Amazon EBS snapshots of the database volume and restores them to launch temporary database instances in an alternate Availability Zone.\n\nDuring testing, database administrators report that the newly launched instances suffer from severe I/O latency spikes and query timeouts during the first few hours of operation. An investigation reveals that this performance degradation occurs because storage blocks are being lazily loaded from Amazon S3 upon initial access. A solutions architect must ensure that volumes restored from the snapshot deliver their full provisioned performance immediately upon creation with the least operational overhead.\n\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?",
