    question_en: "MythicByte Games, a mobile game development studio, runs the matchmaking and session management backend for a multiplayer battle arena game on Amazon EC2 instances within an Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). During weekend in-game events, player traffic surges cause several EC2 instances to experience memory exhaustion and crash due to out-of-memory (OOM) errors. The Auto Scaling group currently scales dynamically based on average CPU utilization, which remains below 40% during these events, preventing scale-out events from triggering. A solutions architect must design a solution that automatically scales out the instance fleet based on memory consumption and sends an Amazon SNS notification to the operations team whenever average memory utilization exceeds 80%.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?",
