    question_en: "CarePulse Health, a digital healthcare startup, operates a cloud-based electronic health records (EHR) platform used by outpatient clinics in the us-east-1 Region. The application tier runs on Amazon EC2 instances across multiple Availability Zones behind an Application Load Balancer. However, the database tier consists of a single-AZ Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL DB instance deployed in us-east-1a.\n\nDuring a recent scheduled maintenance window followed by localized hardware degradation in us-east-1a, clinical staff experienced 45 minutes of unexpected downtime and were unable to access urgent patient charts. A solutions architect must re-architect the database tier to ensure high availability and automatic failover during Availability Zone disruptions and routine maintenance, while minimizing operational overhead.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements?",
