    question_en: "A healthcare records startup is developing a centralized event-driven architecture to process patient-related updates emitted by various clinical microservices. The microservices generate JSON-formatted events that include an `eventType` field (such as `CRITICAL_LAB_RESULT`, `BILLING_UPDATE`, and `APPOINTMENT_SCHEDULED`).\n\nThe startup has the following requirements:\n- Events with `eventType` set to `CRITICAL_LAB_RESULT` must immediately invoke an AWS Lambda function to alert on-call physicians.\n- Events with `eventType` set to `BILLING_UPDATE` must be sent to an Amazon SQS queue for asynchronous batch processing.\n- Events with `eventType` set to `APPOINTMENT_SCHEDULED` must trigger an AWS Step Functions state machine to coordinate patient follow-up communication workflows.\n- The routing mechanism must evaluate event payload contents, deliver events only to matching destinations, and require the least operational overhead.\n\nWhich solution should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements?",
