    question_en: "A healthcare startup named TheraVault operates an electronic health record (EHR) management platform on AWS. The architecture consists of an Application Load Balancer (ALB) deployed across public subnets, a web application tier running on Amazon EC2 instances in private subnets managed by an Auto Scaling group, and an Amazon Aurora MySQL database deployed in dedicated database subnets.\n\nDuring a security review, the operations team identifies two urgent requirements:\n1. Immediately block all incoming traffic originating from a known malicious IP address (198.51.100.77/32) that has been attempting brute-force attacks against the application.\n2. Ensure that the database tier only accepts inbound database traffic on port 3306 from the web application EC2 instances, while seamlessly supporting dynamic auto-scaling events without manual administrative intervention.\n\nWhich combination of actions should a solutions architect recommend to satisfy these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?",
