    question_en: "A regional airline operates a flight reservation and ticketing platform on AWS. The platform's backend application runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer and uses an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL Multi-AZ DB instance as its primary database.\n\nDuring seasonal flash promotions, website traffic surges as hundreds of thousands of passengers search for flight schedules, compare fare classes, and check real-time seat availability. These read-intensive queries cause severe CPU and I/O contention on the RDS DB instance. Consequently, passengers attempting to complete seat reservations and process ticket payments experience high latency and occasional transaction timeouts.\n\nA solutions architect must resolve the database performance bottleneck and ensure that transactional write operations remain responsive during traffic spikes, with minimal operational overhead and without re-architecting the database engine.\n\nWhich solution should the solutions architect recommend?",
