    question_en: "A healthcare technology startup, VitaLogix Health, is developing a cloud-based electronic health record (EHR) management platform. Whenever a patient record is modified, three separate downstream microservices must process the same update event: a compliance auditing service that archives records to long-term storage, an AI clinical analysis engine that extracts medical terminology, and an emergency notification service that alerts care teams.\n\nEach microservice operates at a different processing speed, and the AI analysis engine occasionally experiences traffic spikes that cause processing delays. The startup requires a decoupled, highly available architecture that ensures no update events are lost during sudden traffic surges or if a downstream microservice becomes temporarily unavailable.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?",
