    question_en: "A healthcare startup runs an electronic health records (EHR) platform on AWS. The web tier consists of Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB), and the database tier uses an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL Multi-AZ DB instance. During morning clinic hours, medical staff frequently view and search the same patient immunization records and allergy profiles, resulting in a spike in database CPU utilization above 90% and increased query latency.\n\nA solutions architect must implement a caching solution to offload repetitive read requests from the database, deliver sub-millisecond response times, and provide high availability with automatic failover in the event of a node failure.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements?",
