    question_en: "A healthcare records startup named PulseVault manages high-resolution diagnostic imaging files (DICOM) in an on-premises data center. The startup's on-premises network-attached storage (NAS) array is nearing maximum capacity due to rapid user adoption. The legacy PACS (Picture Archiving and Communication System) imaging applications run on-premises and require access to files via standard file protocols (NFS/SMB) without any application code changes. Radiologists require low-latency access to imaging studies performed within the past 30 days. Files older than 30 days must be securely preserved for several years to satisfy regulatory compliance requirements at the lowest cost.\n\nWhich solution should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?",
