    question_en: "A regional airline, Cascadia Skyways, operates its flight booking platform on AWS. The airline is integrating with an external travel aggregator, VoyageGrid, which runs a multi-tenant SaaS application in its own AWS account. VoyageGrid requires continuous, automated programmatic read access to an Amazon S3 bucket in Cascadia Skyways' account that stores daily seat availability manifests and promotional fare tables.\n\nCascadia Skyways' security compliance team mandates the following requirements:\n- No long-term credentials, such as IAM user access keys, may be created, shared, or stored.\n- VoyageGrid must only receive temporary, automatically expiring credentials when performing data retrieval.\n- The configuration must protect Cascadia Skyways against the confused deputy problem.\n\nWhich solution should a solutions architect recommend to satisfy these requirements?",
