    question_en: "A regional airline, Cascade Air, operates an online flight booking and mobile check-in platform on AWS. When passengers complete online check-in, the system generates primary high-resolution boarding pass PDFs and stores them in Amazon S3 Standard. To enable rapid boarding barcode rendering on handheld mobile scanners used by gate agents across 45 regional airports, an automated background task generates compressed QR-code image thumbnails and stores them in a separate S3 bucket.\n\nThe QR-code thumbnails are retained for 60 days following the flight and are accessed infrequently after generation. However, when gate agents scan a passenger's boarding pass at the gate, the thumbnail image must be retrieved immediately with millisecond latency. If an Availability Zone failure occurs and causes any thumbnail images to be lost, the application can automatically regenerate them within seconds from the primary boarding pass PDFs stored in S3 Standard.\n\nA solutions architect must recommend a storage class for the QR-code thumbnail images that meets these requirements MOST cost-effectively.\n\nWhich Amazon S3 storage class should the solutions architect recommend?",
