    question_en: "A regional airline is modernizing its flight reservation and passenger booking platform. The airline currently maintains 35 TB of historical booking archives, passenger flight manifests, and ticketing logs on an on-premises Network File System (NFS) storage server. An existing 1 Gbps AWS Direct Connect connection connects the on-premises data center to the airline's AWS environment with substantial unused bandwidth.\n\nA solutions architect must design a solution to migrate this data to an Amazon S3 bucket. The solution must perform an initial transfer of the historical data, followed by automated, daily incremental synchronization of new and modified records until the on-premises reservation system is completely decommissioned. The solution must also provide built-in data integrity verification and require the least operational overhead.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements?",
