    explanation_en: "Option C (Index 2) is correct. AWS DataSync is an online bulk data transfer service designed to simplify, automate, and accelerate moving data between on-premises storage systems (such as NFS, SMB, and HDFS) and AWS storage services (Amazon S3, Amazon EFS, and Amazon FSx). Because the airline has an existing 1 Gbps AWS Direct Connect connection with ample available bandwidth, an online transfer service is ideal. DataSync uses a specialized software agent deployed in the on-premises environment, provides automated end-to-end data integrity verification using checksums, and includes built-in scheduling to run daily incremental synchronizations (copying only changed files) with minimal operational overhead.\n\nOption A is incorrect. AWS Storage Gateway (S3 File Gateway) is a hybrid cloud storage service designed to provide on-premises applications with low-latency, cached access to Amazon S3 via standard NFS and SMB protocols. It is designed for ongoing hybrid access rather than as a dedicated, automated bulk migration and scheduled synchronization tool for existing on-premises NFS file servers.\n\nOption B is incorrect. AWS Snowball Edge is a physical data transport appliance intended for offline data migration when network bandwidth is limited, unavailable, or cost-prohibitive. Since the airline already has a dedicated 1 Gbps Direct Connect connection with substantial unused capacity, an offline device is unnecessary. Furthermore, Snowball Edge cannot perform automated daily incremental synchronizations, and implementing custom Lambda functions over a VPN introduces substantial operational complexity.\n\nOption D is incorrect. Although AWS Transfer Family provides fully managed SFTP/FTPS endpoints backed by Amazon S3, using it for this scenario requires writing, testing, and maintaining custom scripts and cron jobs on the on-premises servers to manage incremental file detection, upload retries, and data verification, which introduces high operational overhead."
